  "worked_solution": "The difference formula for sine gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}R\\operatorname{sin}\u2061(x-\u03d5) & =R(\\operatorname{sin}\u2061x\\operatorname{cos}\u2061\u03d5-\\operatorname{cos}\u2061x\\operatorname{sin}\u2061\u03d5) \\\\  & =R\\operatorname{cos}\u2061\u03d5\\operatorname{sin}\u2061x-R\\operatorname{sin}\u2061\u03d5\\operatorname{cos}\u2061x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, by writing the given expression in the amplitude-phase form\n\n$$\n3\\operatorname{sin}\u2061x-4\\operatorname{cos}\u2061x=R\\operatorname{sin}\u2061(x-\u03d5),\n$$\n\nwe get the following identity:\n\n$$\n3\\operatorname{sin}\u2061x-4\\operatorname{cos}\u2061x=(R\\operatorname{cos}\u2061\u03d5)\\operatorname{sin}\u2061x-(R\\operatorname{sin}\u2061\u03d5)\\operatorname{cos}\u2061x\n$$\n\nEquating the coefficients of $\\operatorname{sin}\u2061x$ and $\\operatorname{cos}\u2061x,$ we get the following system of equations:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}R\\operatorname{cos}\u2061\u03d5=3 \\\\ R\\operatorname{sin}\u2061\u03d5=4\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSquaring the first and the second equations of the system and adding the results together, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{(R\\operatorname{cos}\u2061\u03d5)}^{2}+{(R\\operatorname{sin}\u2061\u03d5)}^{2} & ={3}^{2}+{4}^{2} \\\\ {R}^{2}({cos}^{2}\u2061\u03d5+{sin}^{2}\u2061\u03d5) & =9+16 \\\\ {R}^{2} & =25 \\\\ R & =5.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNote that we only consider the positive root since $R>0.$",
